        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-10-15T02:33:42+00:00",
        "description": "<p>Well, after 15 years of saying \"Someday I'll turn this into a web app,\" I finally did it!<p>I've been maintaining a popular repo of terminal themes at <a href=\"https://github.com/mbadolato/iTerm2-Color-Schemes\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/mbadolato/iTerm2-Color-Schemes</a>, and it was finally time to build the app with all the features I wanted!<p>So, the next-gen version is live at <a href=\"https://terminalthemes.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://terminalthemes.com</a>! It currently has over 800 themes, and provides downloads for close to 40 different formats (iTerm, Ghostty, Windows, and many more)<p>It's free for everyone. An account is not needed to browse and download, but registering for an account (free) allows you to vote, bookmark, submit themes, etc.<p>I focused on a11y features for those who need it, in addition to adding Find My Theme and other tools to make it easy to find something you like!<p>Live terminal and code previews help show a more realistic view of the term",
